   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicator 1.1.1.  # of partnerships of VET colleges, public schools, municipalities and other service providers institutionalised and function to provide access to needs-based, targeted and diversified VET to all in formal and non-formal education settings in target regions.
Indicator 1.1.2. # of Special targeted programmes for youth, including NEETs and vulnerable groups, developed and introduced through new types of formal and non-formal education-related services in six (6) target regions.
Indicator 1.2.1. # of VET institutions in six (6) regions that comply with authorization standards, transformed, human resources prepared, and provide high quality programmes and services for skills development. 
Indicator 2.1.1. #  of designed new, high quality, innovative, distance and blended programmes that contribute to the development of key competencies of youth, leading to higher employment rate of participants. 
Indictor 2.1.2: # of new, high quality, innovative, distance and blended programmes implemented
Indicator 2.1.3 Rate of increase employment of  youth, which undertook   distance and blended programmes</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2020">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Baseline 1.1.1. Absence of cooperation, between actors involved in VET in target areas 
Baseline 1.1.2. Absence of targeted modalities and VET programmes and services to youth, NEETs and vulnerable groups.
Baseline 1.2.1. None of existing institutions complying with   authorization standards in target areas
Baseline 2.1.1. Limited opportunities for youth to acquire key competencies, including digital and entrepreneurial skills.
Baseline 2.1.2: Non-existence of distance and blended programmes in target areas
Baseline 2.1.3: Absence of employed youth through this project in target areas</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
